      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely! Some key socio-economic indicators of neighborhood revitalization include increased property values, a rise in new businesses (especially chain stores), more investment in public spaces and infrastructure, an influx of residents with higher incomes, improvements to housing quality, and reduced incidences of crime. Additionally, changes in demographics, such as an uptick in young professionals and families moving into the area, can also be an indicator. It's important to remember that while these changes can signal improvement, they can also sometimes lead to gentrification, which might displace long-time residents.",
